# Build-context filter for image/Containerfile. podman reads .containerignore, docker
# reads .dockerignore; the two files are kept identical. The context is what
# `cargo build --locked` needs (the workspace, desktop/shell and desktop/theme included),
# image/ and the desktop tree that image/install-desktop.sh places (desktop/ stays in;
# its tests do not). *.md is excluded, so desktop/**/README.md never ships either.
.git
.github
.claude
target
**/target
assets
experiments
examples
docs
desktop/tests
*.md
.tamperward
